# @prabhixtechnologies/* lives on GitHub Packages, not npmjs.
#
# Only the registry mapping is here. The token deliberately is not: locally it comes from
# ~/.npmrc, and in CI actions/setup-node writes one from NODE_AUTH_TOKEN. Committing
# `_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` was the other option and it breaks every install where that
# variable is unset, which is every local one.
#
# GitHub Packages requires a token even though these packages are public and this repository can
# read them anonymously on the web. That is the registry's behaviour, not a permission to fix.
@prabhixtechnologies:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
